---@class cloudflare.user.UpdateTokenResponse
---@field id? string|distilled.Null Token identifier tag.
---@field condition? cloudflare.user.TokensUpdateResponseCondition|distilled.Null
---@field creator_email_at_creation? string|distilled.Null The email address of the user who created the token at the time of creation. Only present for Account Owned API Tokens when a creator email was available.
---@field expires_on? string|distilled.Null The expiration time on or after which the JWT MUST NOT be accepted for processing.
---@field issued_on? string|distilled.Null The time on which the token was created.
---@field last_used_on? string|distilled.Null Last time the token was used.
---@field modified_on? string|distilled.Null Last time the token was modified.
---@field name? string|distilled.Null Token name.
---@field not_before? string|distilled.Null The time before which the token MUST NOT be accepted for processing.
---@field policies? cloudflare.user.TokensUpdateResponsePoliciesList|distilled.Null List of access policies assigned to the token.
---@field provisioner_id? string|distilled.Null The identifier of the service that provisioned the token. For an OAuth-provisioned token, this is the OAuth client identifier. Present when `provisioner_type` is present and null when the identifier is unavailable.
---@field provisioner_type? string|distilled.Null The type of service that provisioned the token. Only present for provisioned Account Owned API Tokens.
---@field status? cloudflare.user.TokensUpdateResponseStatus|distilled.Null Status of the token.
---@field token_prefix? string|distilled.Null The prefix of the token value, before the first underscore. Use it with `token_suffix` to identify a token. Only present for tokens created or rolled after this field was added.
---@field token_suffix? string|distilled.Null The last 4 characters of the token value. Use it with `token_prefix` to identify a token. It is not unique. Only present for tokens created or rolled after this field was added.

